B: Yes, I did. Moving to a new school can be really hard.
A: Exactly. I still remember how lonely I felt on my own first day.
B: Let''s do something kind. We could show her around at lunch.
A: Great idea. I can introduce her to the football club too.
B: And I''ll save her a seat right next to us in class.
A: Perfect. One small gesture might make her whole week.
B: You''re right. Let''s make sure she feels truly welcome.', 'A 听说明天有新同学转来;B 说转学很不容易;A 还记得自己第一天有多孤单;两人决定做点好事:午饭时带她参观、把她介绍给足球社、给她在班里留座位;希望一个小举动能让她感到被欢迎。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is joining the class tomorrow?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A new student.","A new teacher.","An old friend.","A school nurse."]},{"q":"How did speaker A feel on her own first day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Excited.","Lonely.","Angry.","Proud."]},{"q":"What does speaker B offer to do in class?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Save her a seat nearby.","Lend her a book.","Carry her bags.","Write her a letter."]},{"q":"What will speaker A introduce the new student to?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The library.","The football club.","The art room.","The music band."]},{"q":"What do the two friends hope their kindness will do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Win them a school prize.","Get them out of class.","Make the new student feel welcome.","Make the teacher happy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');
Do not wait for other people to come to you first.
A warm smile and a friendly hello can open the door to a new friendship.
When you meet someone new, ask about their hobbies and really listen to the answer.
Small acts of kindness, like sharing a snack or lending a pen, help people feel close to you.
Remember, every good friend was once a stranger.', '一个交朋友的小贴士:别等别人先来找你;一个温暖的微笑和友好的问候就能打开新友谊的大门;遇到新朋友时问问他们的爱好并认真倾听;像分享零食、借支笔这样的小善举能拉近彼此;记住,每个好朋友最初都是陌生人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the tip say you should not do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Smile at new people.","Ask about hobbies.","Share your snacks.","Wait for others to come to you first."]},{"q":"What can open the door to a new friendship?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A warm smile and a friendly hello.","An expensive gift.","A long letter.","A loud voice."]},{"q":"When you meet someone new, what should you do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Talk only about yourself.","Ask about their hobbies and listen.","Walk away quickly.","Stay completely silent."]},{"q":"What is given as an example of a small act of kindness?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Winning a game.","Telling a joke.","Sharing a snack or lending a pen.","Singing a song."]},{"q":"What was every good friend once, according to the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A teacher.","A neighbour.","A classmate.","A stranger."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');
B: To me, a true friend is someone who stays when times are hard.
A: So you agree that a friend in need is a friend indeed?
B: Absolutely. Almost anyone can share the good times with you.
A: How do you keep a friendship strong over the years?
B: By being honest and always making time for each other.
A: That''s wonderful. Thank you for sharing your thoughts.
B: My pleasure. Good friends really are one of life''s greatest gifts.', '采访友谊话题:B 认为真朋友是在困难时仍留在你身边的人;同意''患难见真情'';因为顺境时几乎谁都能陪你;维系友谊靠诚实和总愿为彼此花时间;最后说好朋友是人生最珍贵的礼物之一。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"To the interviewee, who is a true friend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Someone who stays during hard times.","Someone who is very rich.","Someone who lives nearby.","Someone who is always funny."]},{"q":"Which saying does the interviewer mention?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Better late than never.","A friend in need is a friend indeed.","Practice makes perfect.","Honesty is the best policy."]},{"q":"According to the interviewee, who can share the good times?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only family members.","No one at all.","Almost anyone.","Only old friends."]},{"q":"How does the interviewee keep a friendship strong?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By giving expensive gifts.","By winning arguments.","By staying very busy.","By being honest and making time."]},{"q":"What does the interviewee call good friends at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["One of life''s greatest gifts.","A waste of time.","A heavy duty.","A small problem."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');
When your friend is talking, give them your full attention instead of looking at your phone.
Try not to break in before they have finished speaking.
If you are not sure what they mean, repeat their idea in your own words to check.
Showing that you truly understand makes your friend feel valued.
Good listening is a quiet but very powerful gift.', '做好朋友的最佳方式之一是做个好的倾听者:朋友说话时全神贯注,别看手机;别在他们说完前打断;不确定意思时用自己的话复述以确认;让对方感到你真的理解,他就会觉得被重视;善于倾听是一份安静而强大的礼物。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is one of the best ways to be a good friend?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To give lots of advice.","To be a good listener.","To talk the most.","To buy nice gifts."]},{"q":"What should you do while your friend is talking?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Check your phone.","Look out of the window.","Give them your full attention.","Start your own story."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say you should try not to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Smile at your friend.","Sit close to them.","Nod your head.","Break in before they finish."]},{"q":"What can you do if you are unsure of your friend''s meaning?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Repeat their idea in your own words.","Change the subject.","Stop listening.","Pretend to agree."]},{"q":"How does good listening make a friend feel?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Bored.","Valued.","Worried.","Angry."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');
B: Not really. I''ve been so lonely here that I''m thinking of leaving school.
A: Please don''t drop out. Give it a little more time.
B: But I don''t have a single friend in this place.
A: You do now. Come and hang out with us this weekend.
B: Really? You''d actually want me to join you?
A: Of course. A new place always feels hard at first.
B: Thank you. Maybe I''ll stay and give it another chance.', 'A 见 B 情绪低落;B 说太孤单,想退学;A 劝他别退学,再给点时间;B 说在这里一个朋友都没有;A 说现在有了,这周末来一起玩;B 很意外;A 说新环境一开始总是难;B 决定留下再试一次。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is speaker B thinking of doing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Joining a club.","Moving house.","Leaving school.","Taking an exam."]},{"q":"Why does speaker B feel this way?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He has failed a test.","He is tired of homework.","He is moving abroad.","He has been lonely with no friends."]},{"q":"What does speaker A ask B not to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Drop out of school.","Skip lunch.","Miss the match.","Phone his parents."]},{"q":"What does speaker A invite B to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Study together tonight.","Hang out with them this weekend.","Join the football team.","Talk to the teacher."]},{"q":"What does speaker B decide at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To leave the next day.","To stop talking to A.","To stay and try again.","To change classes."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');
A good friend listens when we are sad, laughs with us when we are happy, and stands by us when others walk away.
Yet we often forget to say a simple thank-you.
Why not tell your friends today how much you really care?
A few kind words cost nothing, but they can make a friendship last a lifetime.
Cherish the friends you have.', '我们往往要等朋友离开才意识到他们有多重要;好朋友在我们难过时倾听,在我们快乐时同笑,在别人离开时仍守在身边;可我们常忘了说一句简单的谢谢;何不今天就告诉朋友你有多在乎?几句善言不花一分钱,却能让友谊持续一生;珍惜你拥有的朋友。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When do we often notice how much friends mean to us?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["When we are rich.","When we are young.","When we move house.","When they are gone."]},{"q":"What does a good friend do when we are sad?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Listens to us.","Laughs at us.","Walks away.","Stays silent."]},{"q":"What do we often forget to say to our friends?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Goodbye.","A simple thank-you.","A clever joke.","A long story."]},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest doing today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buying a present.","Writing a long letter.","Telling friends how much you care.","Making new friends."]},{"q":"What can a few kind words do, according to the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Cost a lot of money.","Cause an argument.","Be quickly forgotten.","Make a friendship last a lifetime."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective3' AND unit='U2';

International Friendship Day is coming soon, and I am writing to say a heartfelt thank-you. Since the day I moved to this school, you have been the kindest friend I could ever hope to have. I am so glad to have met you on that very first morning.

I will never forget the day you helped me carry my heavy bags home in the rain, or the many times you cheered me up before exams. You always seemed to be standing right beside me whenever I felt low. Such small acts of kindness mean more than you know.

Thank you for everything. I truly cherish our friendship.

Best wishes,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["I am so glad to have met you on that very first morning.","You always seemed to be standing right beside me whenever I felt low.","I will never forget the day you helped me carry my heavy bags home in the rain.","Such small acts of kindness mean more than you know."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"I am glad to meet you last year.","correct":"I am glad to have met you last year.","note":"感激的是过去已完成的相遇,用完成式不定式 to have met。"},{"wrong":"You seemed to stand beside me at that moment.","correct":"You seemed to be standing beside me at that moment.","note":"当时正在进行的动作,用进行式不定式 to be standing。"},{"wrong":"Thank you for help me so much.","correct":"Thank you for helping me so much.","note":"介词 for 后用动名词 helping。"}]'::jsonb, '【感谢信结构】
问候:Dear Anna,
第1段 表达感激:I am writing to say thank-you. I am glad to have met you.
第2段 具体事例:I will never forget the day you … You always seemed to be …
结尾:Thank you for everything. Best wishes, Li Hua', 2, 'elective3', 'U2', 'sufe');

